WEBVTT

00:57:58.625 --> 00:58:00.226
or even a social event, right?

00:58:00.250 --> 00:58:03.393
You're only thinking about everything
that could have been better.

00:58:03.417 --> 00:58:06.726
Well, why not be thrilled about
all the horrible jobs you didn't take,

00:58:06.750 --> 00:58:08.476
all the toxic cultures you avoided,

00:58:08.500 --> 00:58:11.434
all of the difficult bosses
you didn't get stuck working for?

00:58:11.458 --> 00:58:14.226
And that joy of missing out
for me is something

00:58:14.250 --> 00:58:17.393
that probably sticks in my head
on a daily basis.

00:58:17.417 --> 00:58:19.268
With that, I am feeling a little FOMO

00:58:19.292 --> 00:58:21.518
that we're not going to hear
from the audience.

00:58:21.542 --> 00:58:23.184
So let's open it up.

00:58:23.208 --> 00:58:25.018
Woman 1: Thanks, guys.

00:58:25.042 --> 00:58:28.309
I think we all thought
that the autonomy versus loyalty

00:58:28.333 --> 00:58:30.559
was a really eye-opening
and powerful concept.